From 7bd65cc4d16b400c5134d9b16a3da746a147acf2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tung Son Do <dosontung007@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 23:40:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] feat(mcp): add mcp.enabled to start no MCP server in a
 session

With mcp.enabled set to false a session discovers and connects no MCP
server from any source: neither the user's mcp.json nor a project or
third-party config. It creates no MCP manager, so plugin reloads and
mcp_action have nothing to rediscover, and the mcp_test, mcp_add and
mcp_reauth probes and /mcp test, resources and prompts refuse instead
of spawning the server. Until now only project config could be turned
off; a --tools allowlist alone leaves MCP discovery on. The setting
defaults to true and takes effect when a session starts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
