-If `enableMCP` is false or the session restricts tool names, MCP discovery and manager inheritance are skipped entirely. ACP sessions disable on-disk discovery because their MCP definitions come from the ACP client.
+If `enableMCP` is false, the `mcp.enabled` setting is off, or the session restricts tool names, MCP discovery and manager inheritance are skipped entirely. With `mcp.enabled` off, `mcp_test`, `mcp_add` and `mcp_reauth` probes and `/mcp test|resources|prompts` refuse instead of starting a server. The setting takes effect when a session starts. ACP sessions disable on-disk discovery because their MCP definitions come from the ACP client.
 
